THIRD-PARTY NOTICES

1. W3C Geolocation API
   Specification: https://www.w3.org/TR/geolocation/
   License: W3C Software and Document License
   Use: Browser-native geolocation. No W3C code is bundled.

2. Google Location Services (device-level, indirect)
   On Android devices, the browser Geolocation API may internally delegate
   to Google Location Services. This occurs at the OS level and is outside
   the control of SaveThePaws. Governed by:
   https://policies.google.com/terms
   SaveThePaws does not directly call any Google Maps, Places, or Firebase API.
   No Google API key is embedded in this codebase.

3. Anthropic Claude API (AI image moderation)
   Used for animal photo verification at post submission time.
   Governed by Anthropic's Terms of Service: https://www.anthropic.com/legal/terms
   No user personal data is transmitted to the API — only the submitted photo
   and a classification prompt.

4. PWABuilder (build tooling, not bundled)
   License: MIT
   https://github.com/pwa-builder/PWABuilder

5. Web Push API
   Browser-native push notification standard. No third-party push service
   is bundled in v1. Push delivery is handled via the browser's built-in
   push subscription mechanism.
